 have the guardians of the  galaxy  holiday special coming in late 2022 and  we can presume that's going to be  in december and this particular project  should be a lot of fun  then we have a few that are coming in  2023 that are in pre-production that  don't have official release dates yet  and those are  secret invasion iron heart and armor  wars  all of which are in pre-production right  now now those will most likely come  in the middle of 2023 because starting  2023 we have  ant-man and the wasp quantum mania  coming out on february 17th of 2023  followed by the guardians of the galaxy  vol  3 coming out on may 5th in 2023 so one  of them will probably come out between  ant-man and guardians of the galaxy  one right after guardians of the galaxy  in the middle of the year and then  another at the end of the year  now during the trailer that marvel  studios gave us the other day that  announced release dates for plenty of  new shows  the last marvel project that they  mentioned was the fantastic four but  they did not give us a release date  however since they piled it in with the  other films being released in 2023 we  could assume that it's going to be late  2023 or  possibly very early in 2024. however  more than likely it is going to be late  2023 so we only have about a year and a  half left until the fantastic four  entered the mcu  then of course we have blade which was  announced at san diego comic con in 2019  it's currently in pre-production  although recently it was announced that  its release date will be pushed back so  we don't have a release date for it at  this point in time  we also have the i am groot series  coming which we don't have a release  date for either however both  blade and i am groot will probably be in  2024  and they will be joined by deadpool in  2024  as well as we are getting a deadpool 3  yes with ryan reynolds  yes it is going to be rated r it's in  development right now but we do not have  an official release date  and last but not least for what marvel  has officially announced we have the  wakanda series coming to disney plus  we don't have a release date for it yet  it seems very clear that marvel studios  is going to work on black panther 2  first and then the wakanda series will  probably take place after all of the  events of black panther 2.  now those are all of the projects that  have been officially announced by marvel  studios and if you're thinking that's a  lot of projects  yeah it is however marvel is actually  sitting on a lot of projects that are  currently in pre-development or  development that they haven't announced  yet  this was confirmed by malcolm spellman  the showrunner for the falcon and the  winter soldier when he recently said  that he was surprised by how few  projects marvel studios has actually  announced meaning that he's actually  seen the other projects and was  surprised that marvel studios has not  yet revealed them  this doesn't come as too big of a  surprise as marvel studios president  kevin foggy has already stated that  whatever they've announced they usually  have  six plus years already planned after  those shows  so right now marvel studios has pretty  much already planned all of their movies  and shows out to 2030  and based off of some reports we have a  good idea of what some of those could be  for starters it's been announced that  there are two new captain america  projects in the works  malcolm spellman is actually working on  one right now for sam's captain america  it's also been reported that steve  rogers is actually going to return in  some way shape or form and another  captain america movie based off of the  old steve could be in the works right  now as well  again neither of these are that  surprising considering the massive  success that the falcon and the winter  soldier had  and steve rogers as captain america has  always been really popular  another project that kevin feige has  actually stated that they will be  working on at some point in time if they  aren't already  is nova now they've already kind of set  him up in the mcu  thanos decimated zandar presumably  killing everybody on the planet  including all of the nova corps which  would mean that the nova fours  could go on to richard ryder now then we  have the group  the illuminati an illuminati project has  been reported by a few sources at this  point in time including the illuminati  and geekgossitymag.com  with reports that they could be  introduced in doctor strange in the  multiverse of madness perhaps in a  post-credits scene if not not too long  after the movie  the midnight suns have also been  reported to come to the mcu relatively  soon and considering the fact that  marvel is releasing blade  moon knight a rated r deadpool they're  kind of going to introduce sort of a  monster verse inside of the mcu with  some darker characters that i think a  lot of people are really going to enjoy  then of course a thunderbolts and dark  avengers team  we've got reports that both of these  teams are coming to the mcu for some  time now but especially  after the falcon and the winter soldier  people have been wondering when  exactly are the thunderbolts going to be  set up or the dark avengers team  well according to grace randolph at  beyond the trailer they are going to be  two separate teams and marvel is  currently working on both of them  right now of course we have a mutants  project coming  kevin feige announced the mutants were  coming at 2019 san diego comic con  and not much has really been heard about  them since except for about a couple of  months ago it was reported that the  project is currently being worked on and  then we have the famous  wolverine anthology series that is  reportedly coming as well  this project will reportedly explore  wolverine from the very beginning in his  weapon x years  up until whatever they have planned for  him in the upcoming mcu  and of course last but not least you  know it's coming a new  avengers team now marvel is introducing  a lot of new teams like the thunderbolts  the fantastic four  the mutants but they're not going to  forget about the avengers  and it actually looks like sam is set up  quite nicely to be the leader of the new  avengers and of course we'll be getting  another avengers movie at some point  down the line  now these are only a handful of movies  that have been reported there are  definitely a  ton more projects that marvel studios  has yet to announce  since kevin feige said that they  essentially have the next eight years  planned that's over  50 marvel studios projects that we have  no idea what they are  so if you were excited about the mcu  before it's about to get a lot more  exciting within the next couple of years  but in the meantime let me know which  marvel project you are most excited  about  in the comments down below don't forget  to subscribe to stay up to date on the  latest marvel news don't forget to like  the video and for live updates you can  follow  me on instagram and twitter as always  thank you all so much for watching  woof

